    "title": "Saint Leo Lions, featuring ex-Lyman standout Briana Neal, take NCAA Division II Tournament win May 29",
    "text": "Former Lyman High School softball standout Briana Neal helped her current college team, the Saint Leo Lions, secure a 5-3 victory over the Cal State San Marcos Cougars on Friday, May 29, in the NCAA Division II Tournament.\nCompetition was held at Jim Frost Stadium, with a 9 a.m. start.\nThe Lions are scheduled to play again on Sunday, May 31, at 11 a.m. at Jim Frost Stadium.\nBriana Neal — Second baseman — Senior — 5′6″ — Hometown: Sanford",
